 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571529 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186572271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571529 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571529 #edb/ref 1045 "Determining Properties of Objects Described as Functions of Displacement" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571529 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186572271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571529 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571529 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571529 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "9c47e8cc-ad7c-5b83-9c9a-e2bee08c10d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571594 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571594 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571594 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2011be0c-38a3-5056-adae-7b634e1eedc8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571608 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571608 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571608 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "28c22842-c3ce-5a8a-ab8f-72781a08e807" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571621 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571621 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571621 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "31676b05-5ecf-5507-afe8-70e418952d68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571758 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571758 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571758 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7fa15e1a-d450-5bdf-ab2e-7db7463df9ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571846 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571846 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571846 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b0866692-8ed1-5f90-8e94-da9ca9c8496c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571986 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571986 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571986 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571986 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571986 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571986 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571986 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571986 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186571758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571986 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "07559b22-9501-5406-b1d4-af6af28cc58e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572172 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572172 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163546" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572172 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572172 #edb/ref 1071 "A particle $P$ moves along the positive $x$-axis. When the displacement of $P$ from the origin is $x\\,m,$ the velocity is $v\\,m/s,$ the magnitude of the acceleration is $\\frac{k}{x+1}\\,{m/s}^{2},$ where $k$ is a positive constant, and the acceleration is directed toward $O.$ If $P$ has velocity $v=4\\,m/s$ at the origin and the particle is at rest when its displacement is $({e}^{4}-1)\\,m,$ find the value of $k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572172 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ba2fee1b-3766-585f-9ea4-855819a270ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572172 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/e9/e938c4ba0e20c0714d1cd0ef62fb6596b37341b06d29de4e675981007610e12a.png)\n\nSince the acceleration of the particle $P$ has magnitude $\\frac{k}{x+1}\\,{m/s}^{2}$ and is directed *toward* $O,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}),\n$$\n\nwe can rewrite our equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})=-\\frac{k}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides of the above equation with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})\\text{d}x=\\int (-\\frac{k}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwhich gives the general solution\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}=-k\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+C.\n$$\n\nNow, since $v=4\\,m/s$ when $x=0\\,m,$ we can find the value of the constant $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =-k\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(4)^{2} & =-k\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0+1)+C \\\\ C & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}=8-k\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1).\n$$\n\nFinally, since $v=0\\,m/s$ when $x=({e}^{4}-1)\\,m,$ we can find the value of the positive constant $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =8-k\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2} & =8-k\\operatorname{ln}⁡(({e}^{4}-1)+1) \\\\ k\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{4}) & =8 \\\\ 4k & =8 \\\\ k & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572216 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572216 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2cffda36-0576-57f3-9167-08b4838d2180" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572216 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186496284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572249 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572249 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8bcf8cd4-92a9-5914-84aa-0e48430a0339" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572249 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186365288 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572255 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572255 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a4be8856-166e-5b28-9384-7b08fc3db5da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572255 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186572172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572269 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c8464206-7b26-5ba5-b25a-82075e1f6a55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572269 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186365357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572271 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572271 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d8c82ddc-f5d7-56cd-8ad4